>> title: Padrón Peppers, Air Fryer
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: peppers, padron, air fryer, basket, snack, spanish
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: pimientos de padrón, padron peppers, blistered padron peppers, shishito peppers, air fryer padron
>> servings: 4
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: narrow — they are perfect the minute they collapse and sullen two minutes later, and a blistered pepper does not come back
>> washing-up: the basket

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
Oiled in the basket, salted on the plate, so the basket is the only thing.

>> step: toss with oil in the basket, nothing else
Toss @Padrón peppers{9%oz}(250 g; rinsed and dried) with @olive oil{2%tsp} in a preheated #air fryer basket{}, one layer.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 6–8 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)oiled peppers{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{7%min}.

>> step: toss the basket at four minutes — blistered and collapsed
Toss @&(~1)peppers{} by shaking the basket once.

>> step: salt on the plate you are eating from
Scatter @flaky sea salt{1/2%tsp} over @&(~1)blistered peppers{} with @lemon{1%wedge}.
